{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Let's evaluate the two sigma expressions and see which of them results in $-9 + 0 + 9 + 18$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\displaystyle\\sum_{k=0}^3\\left(4k-9\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\left[4(0)-9\\right]+\\left[4(1)-9\\right]+\\left[4(2)-9\\right]+\\left[4(3)-9\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-9 -5 -1 + 3\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\displaystyle\\sum_{k=1}^4\\left(1-10k\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\left[1-10(1)\\right]+\\left[1-10(2)\\right]+\\left[1-10(3)\\right]+\\left[1-10(4)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-9 -19 -29 -39\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, neither sigma expression is equal to $-9 + 0 + 9 + 18$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Consider the sum $-9 + 0 + 9 + 18$.\n\n**Which expression is equal to the above sum?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\displaystyle\\sum_{k=0}^3\\left(4k-9\\right)$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\displaystyle\\sum_{k=1}^4\\left(1-10k\\right)$","correct":false},{"content":"","correct":true,"isNoneOfTheAbove":true}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":true,"multipleSelect":true,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
